Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mm: count shrinkable GPU pool pages in MemAvailable

The GPU driver keeps pages it has finished with in a pool for
reuse. They hold no data and are freed on demand, but MemAvailable
does not count them. On an APU this pool can reach several GiB, so
tools that compute 'used = MemTotal - MemAvailable' report memory
as used when it is really free for the taking.

Add the pool (NR_GPU_RECLAIM) to the estimate. It is added in full,
without the discount used for slab: every pool page is free and the
TTM shrinker can release all of them.

TTM pools that use dma_alloc don't count their pages as NR_GPU_ACTIVE
and don't remove them from NR_GPU_RECLAIM when freeing them, yet moved
them from NR_GPU_ACTIVE to NR_GPU_RECLAIM on give and back on take, so
NR_GPU_RECLAIM grew forever on those pools. Skip that move for them.

Cap the result at MemTotal minus the reserves, so tools that compute
'used = MemTotal - MemAvailable' never go negative.

---
diff --git a/Documentation/filesystems/proc.rst b/Documentation/filesystems/proc.rst
index fa7a468e8..64437e026 100644
--- a/Documentation/filesystems/proc.rst
+++ b/Documentation/filesystems/proc.rst
@@ -1127,8 +1127,9 @@ MemFree
 MemAvailable
               An estimate of how much memory is available for starting new
               applications, without swapping. Calculated from MemFree,
-              SReclaimable, the size of the file LRU lists, and the low
-              watermarks in each zone.
+              SReclaimable, GPUReclaim, the size of the file LRU lists,
+              and the low watermarks in each zone. It never exceeds
+              MemTotal minus the reserved pages.
               The estimate takes into account that the system needs some
               page cache to function well, and that not all reclaimable
               slab will be reclaimable, due to items being in use. The
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/ttm/ttm_pool.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/ttm/ttm_pool.c
index 1bf37023f..d15c5aea5 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/ttm/ttm_pool.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/ttm/ttm_pool.c
@@ -322,6 +322,15 @@ static void ttm_pool_unmap(struct ttm_pool *pool, dma_addr_t dma_addr,
 		       DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL);
 }
 
+static void ttm_pool_type_gpu_reclaim(struct ttm_pool_type *pt,
+				      struct page *p, long nr)
+{
+	if (pt->pool && ttm_pool_uses_dma_alloc(pt->pool))
+		return;
+	mod_lruvec_page_state(p, NR_GPU_ACTIVE, -nr);
+	mod_lruvec_page_state(p, NR_GPU_RECLAIM, nr);
+}
+
 /* Give pages into a specific pool_type */
 static void ttm_pool_type_give(struct ttm_pool_type *pt, struct page *p)
 {
@@ -341,8 +350,7 @@ static void ttm_pool_type_give(struct ttm_pool_type *pt, struct page *p)
 	rcu_read_unlock();
 
 	atomic_long_add(num_pages, &allocated_pages[nid]);
-	mod_lruvec_page_state(p, NR_GPU_ACTIVE, -num_pages);
-	mod_lruvec_page_state(p, NR_GPU_RECLAIM, num_pages);
+	ttm_pool_type_gpu_reclaim(pt, p, num_pages);
 }
 
 static enum lru_status take_one_from_lru(struct list_head *item,
@@ -367,8 +375,7 @@ static struct page *ttm_pool_type_take(struct ttm_pool_type *pt, int nid)
 	ret = list_lru_walk_node(&pt->pages, nid, take_one_from_lru, (void *)&p, &nr_to_walk);
 	if (ret == 1 && p) {
 		atomic_long_sub(1 << pt->order, &allocated_pages[nid]);
-		mod_lruvec_page_state(p, NR_GPU_ACTIVE, (1 << pt->order));
-		mod_lruvec_page_state(p, NR_GPU_RECLAIM, -(1 << pt->order));
+		ttm_pool_type_gpu_reclaim(pt, p, -(1 << pt->order));
 	}
 	return p;
 }
diff --git a/mm/show_mem.c b/mm/show_mem.c
index b938cbcd7..bacca6f5c 100644
--- a/mm/show_mem.c
+++ b/mm/show_mem.c
@@ -67,6 +67,9 @@ long si_mem_available(void)
 	reclaimable -= min(reclaimable / 2, wmark_low);
 	available += reclaimable;
 
+	available += global_node_page_state(NR_GPU_RECLAIM);
+	available = min_t(long, available, totalram_pages() - totalreserve_pages);
+
 	if (available < 0)
 		available = 0;
 	return available;
